-1525-6503"}, "authorAffiliationDetailsList": {"authorAffiliation": [{"affiliation": "Department of Epidemiology and Biostatistics, Memorial Sloan-Kettering Cancer Center, 307 East 63rd Street, New York, NY 10065, USA. vickersa@mskcc.org"}]}}, {"fullName": "Cronin AM", "lastName": "Cronin", "firstName": "Angel M", "initials": "AM"}, {"fullName": "Elkin EB", "lastName": "Elkin", "firstName": "Elena B", "initials": "EB"}, {"fullName": "Gonen M", "lastName": "Gonen", "firstName": "Mithat", "initials": "M"}]}, "authorIdList": {"authorId": [{"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0003-1525-6503"}]}, "dataLinksTagsList": {"dataLinkstag": ["altmetrics"]}, "journalInfo": {"volume": "8", "journalIssueId": 2500986, "dateOfPublication": "2008 Nov", "monthOfPublication": 11, "yearOfPublication": 2008, "journal": {"medlineAbbreviation": "BMC Med Inform Decis Mak", "title": "BMC medical informatics and decision making", "essn": "1472-6947", "issn": "1472-6947", "nlmid": "101088682", "isoabbreviation": "BMC Med Inform Decis Mak"}, "printPublicationDate": "2008-11-01"}, "pubYear": "2008", "pageInfo": "53", "abstractText": "<h4>Background</h4>Decision curve analysis is a novel method for evaluating diagnostic tests, prediction models and molecular markers. It combines the mathematical simplicity of accuracy measures, such as sensitivity and specificity, with the clinical applicability of decision analytic approaches. Most critically, decision curve analysis can be applied directly to a data set, and does not require the sort of external data on costs, benefits and preferences typically required by traditional decision analytic techniques.<h4>Methods</h4>In this paper we present several extensions to decision curve analysis including correction for overfit, confidence intervals, application to censored data (including competing risk) and calculation of decision curves directly from predicted probabilities. All of these extensions are based on straightforward methods that have previously been described in the literature for application to analogous statistical techniques.<h4>Results</h4>Simulation studies showed that repeated 10-fold crossvalidation provided the best method for correcting a decision curve for overfit. The method for applying decision curves to censored data had little bias and coverage was excellent; for competing risk, decision curves were appropriately affected by the incidence of the competing risk and the association between the competing risk and the predictor of interest. Calculation of decision curves directly from predicted probabilities led to a smoothing of the decision curve.<h4>Conclusion</h4>Decision curve analysis can be easily extended to many of the applications common to performance measures for prediction models. Software to implement decision curve analysis is provided.", "affiliation": "Department of Epidemiology and Biostatistics, Memorial Sloan-Kettering Cancer Center, 307 East 63rd Street, New York, NY 10065, USA. vickersa@mskcc.org", "publicationStatus": "epublish", "language": "eng", "pubModel": "Electronic", "pubTypeList": {"pubType": ["research-article", "Journal Article"]}, "meshHeadingList": {"meshHeading": [{"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Humans"}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Prostatic Neoplasms", "meshQualifierList": {"meshQualifier": [{"majorTopic_YN": "N", "abbreviation": "DI", "qualifierName": "diagnosis"}]}}, {"majorTopic_YN": "Y", "descriptorName": "Diagnostic Tests, Routine"}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Confidence Intervals"}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Logistic Models"}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Probability"}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Predictive Value of Tests"}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Molecular Biology"}, {"majorTopic_YN": "Y", "descriptorName": "Decision Support Techniques"}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Computer Simulation"}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Decision Support Systems, Clinical"}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Male"}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Biomarkers", "meshQualifierList": {"meshQualifier": [{"majorTopic_YN": "N", "abbreviation": "AN", "qualifierName": "analysis"}]}}]}, "chemicalList": {"chemical": [{"name": "Biomarkers", "registryNumber": "0"}]}, "subsetList": {"subset": [{"code": "IM", "name": "Index Medicus"}]}, "fullTextUrlList": {"fullTextUrl": [{"availability": "Open access", "availabilityCode": "OA", "documentStyle": "pdf", "site": "BioMedCentral", "url": "http://www.biomedcentral.com/content/pdf/1472-6947-8-53.pdf"}, {"availability": "Open access", "availabilityCode": "OA", "documentStyle": "html", "site": "BioMedCentral", "url": "http://www.biomedcentral.com/1472-6947/8/53"}, {"availability": "Open access", "availabilityCode": "OA", "documentStyle": "abs", "site": "BioMedCentral", "url": "http://www.biomedcentral.com/1472-6947/8/53/abstract"}, {"availability": "Subscription required", "availabilityCode": "S", "documentStyle": "doi", "site": "DOI", "url": "https://doi.org/10.1186/1472-6947-8-53"}, {"availability": "Open access", "availabilityCode": "OA", "documentStyle": "html", "site": "Europe_PMC", "url": "https://europepmc.org/articles/PMC2611975"}, {"availability": "Open access", "availabilityCode": "OA", "documentStyle": "pdf", "site": "Europe_PMC", "url": "https://europepmc.org/articles/PMC2611975?pdf=render"}]}, "isOpenAccess": "Y", "inEPMC": "Y", "inPMC": "Y", "citedByCount": 1128, "hasReferences": "Y", "hasTextMinedTerms": "Y", "hasDbCrossReferences": "N", "hasPDF": "Y", "hasBook": "N", "hasSuppl": "N", "hasLabsLinks": "Y", "hasData": "N", "license": "cc by", "authMan": "N", "epmcAuthMan": "N", "nihAuthMan": "N", "hasTMAccessionNumbers": "N", "dateOfCompletion": "2009-05-19", "dateOfCreation": "2008-11-28", "dateOfRevision": "2022-04-10", "electronicPublicationDate": "2008-11-26", "firstPublicationDate": "2008-11-26", "firstIndexDate": "2009-12-24", "fullTextReceived